~ intro
Señor Food: So, it's your first day? Welcome to my restaurant. Let me tell you a little about myself.
Señor Food: A few years ago I was let go from Google. Ay, qué desastre. It was devastating.
Señor Food: So I started cooking. And I realized I was pretty good. 
Señor Food: While I cook, I feel in my element. Es una cosa hermosa. So naturally, I decided to share my gift with the world, hence my restaurant.
Señor Food: Cooking has become a way of expression for me. And what better way to express myself than to automate it?! 
Señor Food: In my free time I've created a couple robots to help me around the shop. The people of San Jose love it.
Señor Food: The robots are not very advanced though. So I need your help.
Señor Food: I need training data for my robots. And you have, what, 2 years of experience at Chick Fil A? Perfecto, more than enough.
Señor Food: Do your thing, running the restaurant, and I'll have your every move tracked.
Señor Food: Then I'll feed this training data to my bots.
Señor Food: I hear this is a common practice at Meta: hire people to train their replacements! Genius, ¿no?
Señor Food: Just think of it this way, we are pushing the culinary frontier with the latest advancements in technology. 
Señor Food: Bueno, ya. Enough talking, get to work!
=> END